  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 406.12 Required Source Capacity",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 406.12 Required Source Capacity.\n\n(a) The required minimum total source capacity for non-community water systems shall be not less than 1.5 times the system’s design flow based on a 24-hour day.\n\n(b) If the design flow exceeds 13,500 gpd, the PWS shall have a minimum of 2 active wells or an interconnection to another PWS.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 406) #10613, eff 6-1-14; ss by #14158, eff 12-25-24 (formerly Env-Dw 406.10)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
}
